# Tab Grab

Tab Grab is a Chrome extension that saves tabs you want to come back to, automatically organizes them with AI, and helps you rediscover them later.

People often open tabs intending to read, watch, or work on them later, but those tabs get buried among dozens of others. Tab Grab gives those tabs a dedicated place to go instead of letting them disappear.

## Features

- Save tabs to a dedicated dashboard
- AI-powered tab organization
- AI-generated summaries
- Search saved tabs
- Organize tabs into folders
- Automatically close and save tabs after a timer

## How to Use

1. Open a tab you want to save.
2. Right-click the tab.
3. Select "Send To Dashboard."
4. Tab Grab summarizes and organizes the tab.
5. Open the Tab Grab dashboard to view your saved content.

## Built With

- JavaScript
- HTML
- CSS
- Chrome Extension Manifest V3
- Node.js
- Express
- Google Gemini API
- Chrome Storage API
- Chrome Notifications API

## How It Works

When a user saves a tab, Tab Grab sends the title and URL to the backend. 
The backend uses AI to organize the tab and generate a summary. 
The resulting information is stored locally and displayed on the dashboard.

## Motivation

I built Tab Grab because I frequently found myself opening articles, tutorials,
videos, and other resources with the intention of coming back to them later.
Eventually, I would have dozens of tabs open and lose track of what I actually
wanted to use.

Tab Grab is designed to turn those forgotten tabs into a personal library that
can be organized and rediscovered.

## Installation

1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open Chrome and go to `chrome://extensions`.
3. Enable Developer Mode.
4. Click "Load unpacked."
5. Select the Tab Grab extension folder.
6. Tab Grab will now appear in Chrome.
(HAVE TO HAVE NODE.JS AND JS DOWNLOADED) Since as of submission the extension is still being reviewed for google extensions so just to be safe I'm are submitting like this.
7. In terminal enter the server folder and run: node server.js